{"name":"Mean Girls Lipstick","hex":"#ff00ae","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mean","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To intend.","To have as intentions of a given kind."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Common; general.","Of a common or low origin, grade, or quality; common; humble."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mean"},{"term":"girls","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of girl"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A woman's breasts."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/girls"},{"term":"lipstick","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Makeup for the lips.","A stick of this makeup."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To apply lipstick to; to paint with lipstick."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lipstick"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mean Girls","blocks":[{"text":"Mean Girls is a 2004 American teen comedy film directed by Mark Waters and written by Tina Fey. Produced by Lorne Michaels, it stars Lindsay Lohan as the main character Cady Heron, alongside Rachel McAdams as Regina George. The cast also features Fey, Tim Meadows, Amy Poehler, Ana Gasteyer, Lacey Chabert, Lizzy Caplan, Daniel Franzese, Neil Flynn, Jonathan Bennett, and Amanda Seyfried in her feature film debut. Its plot centers on a naïve teen girl who transfers to a public high school in the United States after years of homeschooling in Africa. She quickly befriends two outcasts and the trio form a plan to exact revenge on the queen bee of an envied clique, known as the \"Plastics\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/ac/Mean_Girls_film_poster.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mean_Girls"},{"title":"Girl","blocks":[{"text":"A girl is a young female human, usually a child or an adolescent. While the term girl has other meanings, including young woman, daughter, or girlfriend regardless of age, the first meaning is the most common one."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Young_girl_smiling_in_sunshine_%282%29.jpg/330px-Young_girl_smiling_in_sunshine_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Girl"},{"title":"Lipstick","blocks":[{"text":"Lipstick is a cosmetic product used to apply color and texture to lips, often made of wax and oil. Different pigments are used to produce color, and minerals such as silica may be used to provide texture. The use of lipstick dates back to early civilizations such as Sumer and the Indus Valley Civilisation, and was popularized in the Western world in the 16th century. Some lipsticks contain traces of toxic materials, such as lead and PFAS, which prompted health concerns and regulation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Applying_red_lipstick_-_model_Eve_Casini.jpg/330px-Applying_red_lipstick_-_model_Eve_Casini.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lipstick"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/ac/Mean_Girls_film_poster.png/250px-Mean_Girls_film_poster.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/ac/Mean_Girls_film_poster.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/ac/Mean_Girls_film_poster.png/250px-Mean_Girls_film_poster.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMean_Girls_film_poster.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Tina_Fey_by_Gage_Skidmore.jpg/500px-Tina_Fey_by_Gage_Skidmore.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wik